{"ticker":"AWK","updated":"2026-10-23T22:39:30Z","profile":{"longName":"American Water Works Company, Inc.","shortName":"American Water Works Company, I","sector":"Utilities","industry":"Utilities - Regulated Water","country":"United States","website":"https://www.amwater.com","fullTimeEmployees":7000,"marketCap":28368564224,"trailingPE":24.740034,"forwardPE":21.728046,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":5.3687673,"pegRatio":2.54,"targetMeanPrice":140.54546,"targetHighPrice":155.0,"targetLowPrice":127.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":11,"recommendationKey":"hold","revenueGrowth":0.062,"earningsGrowth":0.086,"grossMargins":0.61469,"operatingMargins":0.40664002,"profitMargins":0.21347,"totalRevenue":5283999744,"beta":0.569,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":144.14,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":120.57,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NYQ","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":2.5},"summary":"American Water Works Company, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides water and wastewater services in the United States. It offers water and wastewater services on military installations; and undertakes contracts with municipal customers, primarily to operate and manage water and wastewater facilities, as well as offers other related services. The company also operates approximately 80 surface water treatment plants; 520 groundwater treatment plants; 170 wastewater treatment plants; 55,000 miles of transmission, distribution, and collection mains and pipes; 1,200 groundwater wells; 1,800 water and wastewater pumping stations; 1,100 treated water storage facilities; and 75 dams. In addition, it offers water and wastewater services to 14 states serving approximately 3.6 million active customers. The company serves residential customers; commercial customers, including food and beverage providers, commercial property developers and proprietors, and energy suppliers; fire service and private fire customers; industrial customers, such as large-scale manufacturers, mining, and production operations; public authorities comprising government buildings and other public sector facilities, such as schools and universities; and other utilities and community water and wastewater systems. The company was founded in 1886 and is headquartered in Camden, New Jersey.","summary_zh":"American Water Works Company, Inc. 透過其子公司在美國提供供水和廢水處理服務。它為軍事設施提供供水和廢水處理服務；並與市政客戶簽訂合同，主要運營和管理供水和污水處理設施，並提供其他相關服務。該公司還經營約 80 個地表水處理廠； 520個地下水處理廠； 170個污水處理廠； 55,000 英里的傳輸、分配和收集幹線及管道； 1,200口地下水儲存；1,800 個供水和污水泵站；1,100 個處理後的水座水壩；此外，它還向 14 個州提供供水和廢水處理服務，為約 360 萬活躍客戶提供服務。該公司為住宅客戶提供服務；商業客戶，包括食品和飲料提供者、商業房地產開發商和業主以及能源供應商；消防服務和私人消防客戶；工業客戶，例如大型製造商、採礦和生產營運；公共機構，包括政府大樓和其他公共部門設施，例如學校和大學；以及其他公用事業和社區供水和廢水系統。該公司成立於 1886 年，總部位於新澤西州卡姆登。","sector_zh":"公用事業","industry_zh":"公用事業 - 調節水","candles":[{"t":"2025-08-25","o":145.54,"h":146.29,"l":144.07,"c":144.4,"v":854900},{"t":"2025-08-26","o":144.37,"h":144.63,"l":143.05,"c":143.95,"v":1764600},{"t":"2025-08-27","o":143.84,"h":144.96,"l":143.16,"c":144.75,"v":1208800},{"t":"2025-08-28","o":144.2,"h":144.36,"l":142.86,"c":142.93,"v":947800},{"t":"2025-08-29","o":143.08,"h":144.54,"l":142.94,"c":143.51,"v":941300},{"t":"2025-09-02","o":142.99,"h":143.74,"l":140.99,"c":141.41,"v":1018800},{"t":"2025-09-03","o":140.84,"h":141.37,"l":139.81,"c":140.7,"v":1054800},{"t":"2025-09-04","o":141.98,"h":142.45,"l":140.74,"c":141.57,"v":1128400},{"t":"2025-09-05","o":141.99,"h":143.6,"l":141.58,"c":143.6,"v":782200},{"t":"2025-09-08","o":142.65,"h":143.23,"l":139.02,"c":140.02,"v":1331800},{"t":"2025-09-09","o":139.53,"h":140.6,"l":138.73,"c":140.09,"v":725500},{"t":"2025-09-10","o":140.21,"h":140.48,"l":137.53,"c":138.5,"v":990000},{"t":"2025-09-11","o":138.75,"h":139.76,"l":137.67,"c":139.63,"v":926600},{"t":"2025-09-12","o":138.5,"h":139.89,"l":138.21,"c":139.28,"v":994600},{"t":"2025-09-15","o":139.3,"h":139.65,"l":137.24,"c":137.58,"v":1084100},{"t":"2025-09-16","o":137.4,"h":138.3,"l":136.18,"c":136.25,"v":1056000},{"t":"2025-09-17","o":136.84,"h":137.94,"l":135.88,"c":136.09,"v":1024100},{"t":"2025-09-18",